"## Summary\n\nIsolation follow-up 25: F24-01, the whole-node boundary planner's empty added schedule and the reviewer's crash on it. Also the D-098 archive of follow-up 24's root records, and one assembled run in scheduled mode.\n- **Session:** launched 10:27 EST on 2026-11-04 on #475's roadmap row (`2a7065b7`), and delivered at 11:35. It rebased onto `034c82cf` (#476) before the run.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 7 commits and 529 owned files, +574,931/−58,258. Most of it is records: the D-098 archive of 213 files, the diagnosis, the offline replays and the new run's records. The largest file is 1.0 MB, and the total is 46.6 MB.\n  - **The code:**\n    - `tests/e2e/at/isolation/boundaryplan/`, a new pure planner package with its tests;\n    - `observer_main.go`, which now calls it;\n    - `review_boundary.py` and `boundary_evidence_test.py`.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (`1c39a0e7`, after agent-core 52, #477) with this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/at-isolation.mk at-isolation-lint`, `at-isolation-test` and `at-isolation-build`, including the new `boundaryplan` tests. The Go suite also runs both Python test files, and the orchestrator ran them directly as well: 15 tests, OK;\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - the committed-evidence tests (`TestCommitted*` in `tests/netlab`, `tests/e2e` and `tests/e2e/at/...`);\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one assembled run in the lane's own namespace, with no rerun and no reservation. The offline gate waited 751 s for an orchestrator reservation before the run, and the live preflight waited 0 s. All 48 overlap samples were clear. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **D-098 first** (`77067bc7`, with expanded-form pins in `1841bc8e`): run `df9dbad7`'s 213 root, support and reload-stream files are archived byte-identically under `history/follow-up-24/`. Every earlier archive is untouched, `history/follow-up-24-run/` included, and no handover read needed re-pointing.\n- **The diagnosis (D-141) confirms the orchestrator's arithmetic, and places the outlier in the capture reader.**\n  - Packet 56's capture-read transit was 15.176 ms. The next largest of the 103 samples was 0.167 ms.\n  - With the 2.674 ms latency spread, the spacing came to 33.2 ms. Without packet 56 it would have been 3.2 ms. Any spacing above 31.5 ms excludes both the 37 ms and the 63 ms cadence gaps, so all 14 candidates were excluded.\n  - **The independent tcpdump capture shows packet 56 crossing the node in 23 µs.** The member's reply was read 0.48 ms before the calibration reader's ingress read. So the 15.2 ms is capture-read delay, not datapath transit. The reader keeps no syscall-entry or write timing, so the cause of the delay is unestablished.\n  - No Apply, reload guard, renewal or netlink receipt overlaps packet 56. One outstanding desired-state request did, and it ended 502. An outstanding request is not an Apply.\n  - **The sample is kept,** with no discount.\n  - The orchestrator's table of earlier plans agrees. Follow-up 20's plan had no samples and no added-schedule key, so its old reviewer failed with reasons instead of crashing.\n- **The fix** (`57a95003`): the observer now calls one pure Go planner, `boundaryplan.Plan`.\n  - **Unchanged:** the formula, the checkpoint, the calibration inputs, both original cadences, the grid anchor and D-142. `deadline_trace.go` is byte-identical.\n  - **The plan is never silent:**\n    - `added_scheduled_mono_ns` is always an array;\n    - `qualified` is true only when that array is non-empty;\n    - an unqualified plan names its reason, its spacing, the actual cadence gaps, and every excluded candidate with the sends that excluded it.\n  - **The reviewer:**\n    - validates the plan's fields before using them, and keeps every existing check and its wording;\n    - on an unqualified or malformed plan, writes `boundary-review.json` with `status: fail` and `schedule_qualified: false`, and exits 1;\n    - reports the packet verdict separately.\n  - The scheduled summary still reports that exit as an error. F24-01 is not a D-163 entry.\n  - **The offline replays** (`ad88ba99`):\n    - `df9dbad7` now gives an explicitly unqualified empty plan and a complete failed review;\n    - `328ab9e0` and the 11-04 runner give added schedules byte-identical to their originals, 31 and 49 probes, and their reviews still pass;\n    - nine Python tests cover missing, null, empty and non-list schedules, wrongly typed fields, invalid JSON and a missing file.\n  - **The trade-off is deliberate.** An isolated capture-read outlier can still make a future sample unqualified. That blocks the row; it cannot pass it wrongly.\n- **The run:** `bd73d7a4` on `4c495c3b`, which is `main` at `034c82cf` plus this lane's commits. 15:47:50–16:11:27Z, 1,416.6 s, in scheduled mode.\n  - **27 pass, 2 blocked, 0 fail. Exit 0, and the scheduled job passes.**\n  - All 29 statuses match `df9dbad7`.\n  - **Blocked:** AT11's IPv6 platform matrix and AT13's full continuous fault matrix, the two operator matrices.\n- **The whole-node expiry passes, and qualifies under D-142.**\n  - **The plan:** 103 samples, a maximum transit of 1.074 ms, spacing 5.5 ms and no discounts. 34 added probes were planned and observed, 236 in all.\n  - **The packet verdict:** 164 positives and 72 drops. The last positive left at D − 99.869 ms, and the first drop reached ingress at D − 94.561 ms.\n  - **D-142:** qualified, with zero overlaps in the judged tail and none anywhere.\n- **AT13's member expiry passes again,** under follow-up 24's unchanged plan.\n  - The first binding-bearing renewal, generation 29, was issued at A + 22.1 s and seen serving at 16:03:50.28Z.\n  - After the member's deadline, all five requests timed out with bytes flat at 2,629, while all six reads showed the node serving.\n  - The last probe finished 15.5 s before the node's lease expired.\n- **The D-120 lab passes under D-161,** on complete checked captures:\n  - 58 TCP reads and zero TCP timeouts;\n  - seven lost transmissions, each attributed to a guard;\n  - one UDP loss, within D-120's allowance of five per 100 reloads;\n  - longest TCP stall 210.6 ms; 101 verified Applies, with the guard's upper bound at most 57.6 ms.\n- **Node writes:** 15 commands in 15 attempts. Zero conflicts.\n- **Agent restarts:** four restart windows, each with a parent receipt of exit 0 and a matching identity. No watchdog decision was retained in any window, and there is no `baseline_unverified` or `GENERATION_MISMATCH` line. The lane makes no closure claim.\n- **F24-01 closes for the planning record and the reviewer's crash only.**\n  - `df9dbad7` stays failed for its boundary review. Its packet verdict, 161 positives and 41 drops, is unchanged, and its D-142 qualification is not established retroactively.\n  - No product change is credited with this run's smaller transit.\n- **Carried:** AT11's and AT13's operator matrices, and F17-01, still not exercised, under D-163.\n"
